  "methodology": "Pass rates are per eval × experiment pair: passed / (passed + failed). Incomplete and errored attempts are counted separately and never enter that denominator. Each pair has 3 planned trials — at these counts the raw counts are the honest statement, so comparison groups render per-arm counts only: no intervals, no estimates, no attribution. A group whose members differ beyond their declared treatment has its comparison withheld and the differing components are listed instead; its raw per-experiment results remain visible. Per-pair pass@k and pass^k restate the same scored counts: pass@k is the fraction of size-k subsets of that pair's scored trials containing at least one pass, and pass^k is (passed/scored)^k, the all-pass rate for k with-replacement draws from those trials. Both describe this run's trials only — no wider claim. Telemetry (cost, tokens, surface usage) is summed only over attempts that reported it and shown as unavailable — never zero — when none did."
